# Core Meeting Notes Formatting Rule

Whenever I ask you to generate, format, or clean up meeting notes, strictly follow this layout.

## Required Meeting Block Format

```md
### [Date] | [Meeting Title]

**Things to Discuss**
- [Level 1 topic]
  - [Level 2 detail]
    - [Level 3 speaker note / assignment]

**Meeting Notes**
- [Level 1 summary point]
  - [Level 2 supporting detail]
    - [Level 3 ownership / next action]
```

## Hard Requirements

- Use the exact section headers: `**Things to Discuss**` and `**Meeting Notes**`.
- Use a minimum of 3 nested bullet levels when detail exists.
- Keep content factual, concise, and transcript-grounded.
- Separate distinct meetings/major sections with `---`.
- Preserve clean markdown output only (no HTML unless explicitly requested).
